<title>USA: American Radio in radio station swap.</title>
<headline>American Radio in radio station swap.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Radio Systems Corp said Monday it had agreed to swap its radio stations KUDL-FM and WDAF-AM in Kansas City and KCTC-AM in Sacramento plus $3 million cash for privately-held Entertainment Communications Inc's radio station KLOU-FM in St. Louis.</p>
<p>American Radio said the swap would solidify its position in St. Louis and still allow it to maintain a significant Kansas City presence with four remaining FM stations.</p>
<p>The deal requires regulatory approval.</p>
</text>
